<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- config/owasp/suppressions.xml -->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        1. Log4j — bridge only, no Log4j implementation on the classpath
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        spring-boot-starter-logging pulls log4j-to-slf4j, which routes Log4j API
        calls to SLF4J and therefore to Logback. log4j-core is absent, so none of
        the Log4j layouts or appenders exist at runtime.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>False positive — affects log4j-1.2-api bridge only, not log4j-api or log4j-to-slf4j</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.logging\.log4j/log4j.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34479</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress>
        <notes>False positive — affects log4j-1.2-api bridge only, not log4j-api or log4j-to-slf4j</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.logging\.log4j/log4j.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-34477</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress until="2027-06-30">
        <notes>
            Not exploitable — requires JsonTemplateLayout or MapMessage.asJson(),
            both provided by log4j-core, which is not on the classpath. TaskFlow
            logs through Logback via the log4j-to-slf4j bridge and never builds a
            MapMessage. Lift when the Spring Boot BOM ships a log4j2 version above
            2.26.0, or when log4j-core is ever introduced, whichever comes first.
        </notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.logging\.log4j/log4j.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-49844</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        2. MySQL Connector/Net — wrong product, shared CPE identifier
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        Oracle publishes every MySQL driver under the same
        cpe:oracle:mysql_connectors identifier, so Dependency-Check attributes
        Connector/Net advisories to the Java driver. These three target the .NET
        driver, which this project does not embed. The four genuine Connector/J
        advisories were resolved by upgrading to 26.7.0 in this same change.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Wrong product — targets Connector/Net (.NET driver), not Connector/J</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.mysql/mysql-connector-j@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-60193</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress>
        <notes>Wrong product — targets Connector/Net (.NET driver), not Connector/J</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.mysql/mysql-connector-j@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-60192</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress>
        <notes>Wrong product — targets Connector/Net (.NET driver), not Connector/J</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/com\.mysql/mysql-connector-j@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-60317</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        3. Tomcat examples web application — absent from an embedded Tomcat
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-12-31">
        <notes>
            Not applicable — targets the WebSocket chat example web application,
            which ships with the standalone Tomcat distribution and not with
            tomcat-embed-core. Fixed in Tomcat 10.1.58, unreleased as of
            18 Aug 2026. Lift once the tomcat.version override in build.gradle
            reaches 10.1.58 or later.
        </notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        4. Gradle plugin classpath — never shipped to production
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        These four artifacts belong to the build tooling, mostly to the
        Dependency-Check plugin itself. Verified on 18 Aug 2026 by running the
        Gradle dependencyInsight task against the runtimeClasspath configuration
        for each of them: no match is returned, so they are absent from the
        application runtime classpath and from the Docker image. Their versions
        are controlled by the plugins, not by this project. Upgrading the
        Dependency-Check plugin from 12.2.2 to 13.0.0 on 20 August 2026 left all
        five findings in place, so an upgrade is not a remediation path here —
        checked rather than assumed.
    -->
    <suppress until="2027-06-30">
        <notes>Build tooling only — not on runtimeClasspath. Also limited to the async HttpClient, unused here.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.httpcomponents\.client5/httpclient5@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-71290</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-64607</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress until="2027-06-30">
        <notes>Build tooling only — not on runtimeClasspath, no HTTP server exposed by the build</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.httpcomponents\.core5/httpcore5.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54399</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-54428</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress until="2027-06-30">
        <notes>Build tooling only — not on runtimeClasspath, no archive extracted from an untrusted source</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.codehaus\.plexus/plexus-utils@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-67030</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress until="2027-06-30">
        <notes>Build tooling only — not on runtimeClasspath, no external property path reaches PropertyUtilsBean</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/commons-beanutils/commons-beanutils@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2025-48734</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        5. Spring Boot — Cassandra and RabbitMQ SSL, likely obsolete
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        Both were documented as fixed in Spring Boot 3.5.14. The project now runs
        3.5.16, so these two suppressions are probably dead weight. They are kept
        for one report cycle only: removing them is the way to find out, since a
        suppressed finding never appears in the report and absence proves nothing.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-12-31">
        <notes>Cassandra SSL — not exploitable, TaskFlow uses no Cassandra. Verify removal against a 3.5.16 report.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-40974</cve>
    </suppress>
    <suppress until="2026-12-31">
        <notes>RabbitMQ SSL — not exploitable, TaskFlow uses no RabbitMQ. Verify removal against a 3.5.16 report.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.springframework\.boot/.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-40971</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        6. DOMPurify bundled in swagger-ui — no upstream fix reachable
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        Springdoc 2.9.0 brings swagger-ui 5.32.11, which bundles DOMPurify
        3.4.12. That upgrade cleared eighteen of the nineteen identifiers the
        previous swagger-ui 5.21.0 carried; this is the one that survives.

        Not patchable from here. DOMPurify is JavaScript packaged inside the
        swagger-ui jar, not a declared dependency: there is no version property
        to override and no exclusion that would not break Swagger UI outright.
        The fix exists upstream in DOMPurify 3.4.13, but swagger-ui has not
        picked it up, and Springdoc 2.9.0 is already the most recent release on
        the Spring Boot 3.x line.

        Limited exposure. Swagger UI runs DOMPurify over the Markdown
        descriptions of the OpenAPI specification, which this project writes
        itself in its own annotations. Exploiting the flaw would require
        injecting content into that specification, which already implies write
        access to the source. Scored medium, unscored by the NVD, reported by
        RetireJS rather than the NVD feed.

        Counted twice, once per bundle file: swagger-ui-bundle.js and
        swagger-ui-es-bundle.js.

        Lift as soon as a swagger-ui release bundling DOMPurify 3.4.13 or later
        reaches a Springdoc version compatible with Spring Boot 3.5. The short
        expiry is deliberate: this one moves upstream, unlike the suppressions
        above.
    -->
    <suppress until="2026-11-30">
        <notes>
            No upstream fix reachable — DOMPurify is bundled inside the
            swagger-ui jar, not declared as a dependency. Fixed in DOMPurify
            3.4.13, not yet bundled by swagger-ui. Re-evaluate at expiry.
        </notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:javascript/DOMPurify@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-75838</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>
